Subject: select: class-keyed option spacing, chevron and indicator rules

What: select-v2's listbox spaces options with `> .ui-select-v2-option +
.ui-select-v2-option`, the chevron rotates on `.ui-select-v2-chevron` under the
trigger's [data-expanded], and the selected mark shows on the indicator's class;
the original select spaces `.ui-select-select-item` the same way.
Why: `> *:not([role=presentation]) + *:not([role=presentation])` nested under two
attribute-only compounds gives Blink's ancestor filter nothing to reject under any
[data-component]/[data-slot] ancestors, so every element below flags its parent as
affected by `+` rules. The transcript's virtual list sits under both: each row a
scroll added or removed restyled the whole list, 11,664-14,192 elements over a
3,000 px wheel scroll against 5,063-5,073 without the sheet. The chevron and mark
rules keyed on `svg` under `[data-slot]` had the same shape.

